1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,654
Before we put anything into HarnessStation, let's see exactly where it keeps your data on disk.

2
00:00:03,654 --> 00:00:07,000
Once you've seen this folder, nothing in the rest of the course feels like a black box.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,590
Everything lives in one folder in your home directory, called dot-harnessx.

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:13,463
On Windows that's your user profile, backslash dot-harnessx.

5
00:00:13,463 --> 00:00:16,000
Open it and you can see the whole layout at a glance.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,407
Inside, each thing the app manages has its own place: settings, your conversations, presets, snapshots, exports, agent memory, avatars, downloaded models and engines, and a temp folder.

7
00:00:25,407 --> 00:00:28,000
Nothing hidden, nothing proprietary — just folders.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,860
Open any single chat file and you'll see it's plain, readable JSON — your messages, right there in text.

9
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,869
There's no database, no proprietary format.

10
00:00:34,869 --> 00:00:38,000
You can read it, back it up, or move it with an ordinary file copy.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,138
There's one deliberate exception, and it matters.

12
00:00:40,138 --> 00:00:41,753
Your API keys are NOT in this folder.

13
00:00:41,753 --> 00:00:46,771
They live in your operating system's credential store — Windows Credential Manager, or the Secret Service on Linux.

14
00:00:46,771 --> 00:00:50,000
So even someone who copies your dot-harnessx folder doesn't get your keys.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,395
One gotcha to save you grief: don't hand-edit these files while the app is running.

16
00:00:53,395 --> 00:00:56,545
It holds your chats in memory and will overwrite your edits on the next save.

17
00:00:56,545 --> 00:00:59,000
Close the app first if you ever need to touch them directly.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,866
Now that you know where everything lands, let's put something in it — starting with a free local model.

19
00:01:03,866 --> 00:01:05,000
That's the next episode.

